<title>USA: Burlington Cty, N.J., won't back rail line--paper.</title>
<headline>Burlington Cty, N.J., won't back rail line--paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burlington County, N.J., officials have withdrawn their support for a proposed light rail line and defeated a plan to put the matter to voters in November, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Opponents argued that the $1.1 billion rail line would create safety and traffic problems along its route.</p>
<p>NJ Transit's board of directors approved the proposal last year, and have already begun engineering and design work.</p>
<p>((--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652))</p>
